sbook><name>YUTANI NAOKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MITSUBISHI DENKI KABUSHIKI KAISHA</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OHJI, HIROSHI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SAKAI, YUICHI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TSUTSUMI, KAZUHIKO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YUTANI, NAOKI</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>OHJI HIROSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SAKAI YUICHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TSUTSUMI KAZUHIKO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YUTANI NAOKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OHJI, HIROSHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SAKAI, YUICHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TSUTSUMI, KAZUHIKO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YUTANI, NAOKI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A pressure sensor comprises a diaphragm (6) with a first surface that receives pressure, and a thermal detector (3) having a heat-sensitive resistor opposed to the diaphragm with a spacer between. Since the quantity of displacement of the diaphragm due to the change in pressure is detected as the change in the state of heat equilibrium in the thermal detector, the diaphragm surface that receives pressure directly from the fluid for measurement does not require any treatment, such as filming and photochemical treatments. Therefore, main parts of the thermal pressure detector can be made in great quantities on a silicon wafer in a simple manufacturing process. This provides low-cost pressure sensors while improving the accuracy and reliability of thermal pressure detector elements.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un détecteur de pression comprenant une membrane (6) comportant une première surface recevant la pression, et un détecteur (3) thermique pourvu d'une résistance sensible à la chaleur disposé à l'opposé de la membrane, un espace étant ménagé entre la membrane et le détecteur. Etant donné que le déplacement de la membrane sous l'effet du changement de pression est détecté sur la base du changement d'état de l'équilibre thermique au niveau du détecteur thermique, la surface de la membrane recevant directement la pression du fluide à mesurer ne nécessite aucun traitement, à savoir ni traitement filmogène ni traitement photochimique. Par conséquent, les pièces principales du détecteur thermique de pression peuvent être fabriquées en grandes quantités, par un procédé de fabrication simple, sur une plaquette de silicium. On obtient ainsi des capteurs de pression peu coûteux, et les éléments dudit détecteur thermique de pression présentent une précision et une fiabilité améliorées.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>